From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-asus <noreply@github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENTAL: drm/amd/pm: debugfs to send AllowZstates to SMU
 14.0.x APUs

EXPERIMENTAL, NOTHING SENT BY DEFAULT (local carry for ROG Zephyrus G16
GA605KM idle power testing; not submitted upstream).

SMU 14.0.0 firmware defines a driver-mailbox message AllowZstates
(PPSMC_MSG_AllowZstates, 0x25; argument ZStates_e: 0 = disallow, 8 = Z8,
9 = Z9 and Z8) "to inform PMFW of allowing Zstate entry". swsmu has a
generic SMU_MSG_AllowZstates but the 14.0.0 message map has no entry for
it, and nothing in the driver sends it. On the G16 (MP1 14.0.4) every
idlemask bit reads idle at runtime with the screen off, the PSP and the
keyboard xHCI suspended, yet timein_s0i2 stays 0. Static analysis of the
SMU firmware suggests that its runtime deep-idle gate also needs a
Z-state enable that only this message (or the display's
AllowZstatesEntry) appears to feed.

Map SMU_MSG_AllowZstates to PPSMC_MSG_AllowZstates for 14.0.x, and add a
root-only, write-only debugfs file, amdgpu_smu_allow_zstates, in the
device's DRM debugfs directory (MP1 14.0.0, 14.0.1, 14.0.4 and 14.0.5).
Writing 0, 8 or 9 sends the message with that argument; any other value
is rejected with -EINVAL, and -EBUSY is returned during reset or
suspend. Each write logs the result and the argument register the SMU
leaves behind:

  EXPERIMENTAL: SMU AllowZstates(9) sent: 0, arg register 0x...

The message is sent only on an explicit write; nothing else changes.

What the display code sends for AllowZstatesEntry is already logged by
dcn35_smu.c's smu_print() (DC_LOG_SMU), which dynamic debug can turn on:

  echo 'file dcn35_smu.c +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control
